{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>A remnant shall return.</b> It is the name of the prophet's son, and he explained that the meaning of שאר ישוב is upon 'the remnant of Jacob,' which is Judah, and also ישוב governs itself and then what follows it, like מתן בסתר יכפה אף (Proverbs 21:14), and so it is: 'the remnant of Jacob shall return to El Gibbor.'" "And the meaning of <b>Gibbor</b> is because He is able to save them."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:14.188033674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}